The game came a long way but it is still missing some key components, making it a bit dull and repetitive.
It would be great if in the future the following things could be added:

War between races;
Abilities to fight aliens, join alliance, become an enemy;
Cities, bigger and more complex buildings to find.
More NPCS and more quests;
Water physics along with springs, real rivers, waterfalls, underground rivers etc;
Cannyons, creeks, improvement to the a wider variety of terrains.

Reviews.139230:
No Man's Sky is a game I never thought I would play. On one hand it's a typical open world survival game that offers the things you'd expect (crafting, inventory management, etc). There is however a feeling that you really are living another life that not many games can offer. From building and doing missions with your friends, to exploring the cosmos trying to find rare things to sell. While I will say there are a LOT of things I wish this game would add or expand upon, it's already a hugely fun time, especially if you love Sci-fi. There are bugs and visual glitches but for such a small Dev team you can't fault them too much. I've been a player since launch (2016 on PS4) and it's been a wild ride of updates and changes. If you're wanting a game to immersive yourself in and soak up the fantasy of being a space explorer, this is your game.

TLDR; 
Fun, lots of creativity. Has numerous bugs but a very vocal dev team who iron these out. Great for sci-fi/survival fans.
